>> title: Collard Greens, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: greens, southern, pork, side, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: collard-greens
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: greens, collards, turnip greens, mustard greens, mixed greens, pot likker, potlikker, slow cooker collard greens, crockpot collards
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, hot-water-cornbread, black-eyed-peas
>> servings: 8
>> time: 7 hr 20 min
>> slack: forgiving — past six hours it is a difference in colour only, and greens taken that far never come back green
>> washing-up: the slow cooker crock, the skillet, a basin to wash the greens in

Two cups of stock and not three quarts. Greens release a great deal of their own and the pot keeps every drop.

>> step: trim the ribs out, wash in three waters
Trim @collard greens{4%lb}(1.8 kg; thick ribs pulled out, leaves cut in wide ribbons) and wash them in three changes of water until no grit settles.

>> step: render 8 min in a skillet
Render @thick-cut bacon{6%slices}(chopped) in a #skillet{} for ~render{8%min}.

>> step: sweat 6 min
Sweat @&(~1)bacon{} with @yellow onion{1%large}(diced), @garlic{4%cloves}(sliced) for ~sweat{6%min}.

>> step: stew on low, 7 hr
Slow cook @&(~1)pork base{}, @&(~3)washed greens{} with @ham hock stock{2%cup}(475 mL), @cider vinegar{2%Tbs}, @light brown sugar{1%tsp}, @crushed red pepper{1/2%tsp}, @kosher salt{2%tsp}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, @hot sauce{1%Tbs} in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{7%hr}, the greens packed down in handfuls.
